  "limitations": [
    "No Windows process, actual #DB/VEH end-to-end latency, game, GPU/FPS or multiplayer execution in this round.",
    "17-to-1 counts successful tag4 callback game/stack reads only. The resumed strict native leaf still reads CurrentPlayer once.",
    "The ten world checks now refresh at ordinary owner maintenance or a fresh request. A same-frame change before the next boundary may retain the override; no fixed refresh latency or per-hit live equivalence is claimed.",
    "The six target House checks are deliberately removed, not cached. Rejection means continue the original predicate, not force a false game result.",
    "Breakpoint sites and hardware exception hit counts are unchanged; OS exception dispatch and restore costs remain.",
    "Portable lifecycle tests use actual extracted production bodies with modeled Service, memory, clock and exception delivery. The two Windows SEH groups compile/link actual product guards but do not execute Windows.",
    "Controlled Service timings replace Win32/SEH/final-callback boundaries. Raw distributions are retained without promoting their medians to a Windows or game speedup claim.",
    "These eight focused checks cover the current change; they do not claim every repository test passed. Independent review is supporting evidence, not a ninth executed test."
  ],
